  "question": {
    "text": "For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8450;</mi></math>, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8450;</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>Re</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>Im</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8450;</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>Re</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>Im</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo></math>. Then among the two statements:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> : If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Re</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>Im</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> contains all the real numbers<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> : If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Re</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>Im</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> contains all the real numbers,",
    "image": null
  },
